    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials`. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field on the owner API response, following the same pattern the codebase already uses for the computed `displayName` field.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an `initials` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (the OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto` with a getter/setter from this at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the initials as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, each followed by a dot (e.g. `john` + `smith` \u2192 `J.S.`).\n\nThe acceptance test's assertion \u2014 `GET /api/owners/{id}` returning `$.initials == \"J.S.\"` for firstName \"john\"/lastName \"smith\" \u2014 now passes, and the full suite (255 tests) remains green.",
